WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.010
Cutting a piece out of a shape always reduces its area.

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.390
But the perimeter might stay the same, or even grow.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.200
Area and perimeter respond to changes in

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.530
completely different ways.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.220
Questions often ask about perimeter after a cut,

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:17.330
or area after an enlargement.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.300
Each needs its own reasoning, and mixing them up is

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.170
a common mistake.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.470
A five by three rectangle has a one by one square cut

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:26.140
from a corner.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:28.000
What is its perimeter now?

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:31.260
Pause and compare the old boundary with the new.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:36.390
The original perimeter is sixteen.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.270
The cut removes two short pieces of boundary,

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:40.590
each of length one.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:44.570
But it exposes two new pieces, also each of length one.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:46.630
The perimeter is still sixteen.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.580
The new edges can be slid out to replace the

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:50.610
old ones exactly.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.900
Now cut the same square from the middle of

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:54.630
a side instead.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.070
One piece of length one is removed,

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:58.970
but three new pieces appear.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.990
The perimeter rises by two, to eighteen.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.550
Same area removed, different effect on the boundary.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.490
Scaling is a different kind of change.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:12.100
Double every length of a two by three rectangle and you

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.210
get four by six.

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:16.350
The perimeter doubles, from ten to twenty.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:19.900
But the area becomes four times as big, from six to

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:22.220
twenty-four, because both the length and the

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:23.130
width were doubled.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.430
For solids, three directions are scaled.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.680
Doubling every length of a cube makes its volume eight

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:30.550
times as large.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:33.570
Tripling makes it twenty-seven times as large.

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:37.090
For a cut, compare the boundary removed with

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:38.160
the boundary created.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:41.740
For scaling by a factor, lengths multiply by the factor,

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:44.820
areas by its square, and volumes by its cube.

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:48.310
Notebook challenge: a photograph is enlarged so that

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:50.220
every length is three times as long.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:52.660
How many times as large is its area?
